WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.188 --> 00:00:17.970
come back to take you home at half-past five," Dr.

2
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.231
Chilton said, leaving Pollyanna at Mr.

3
00:00:20.271 --> 00:00:21.052
Pendleton's door.

4
00:00:22.853 --> 00:00:25.735
Pollyanna entered the great stone house and found Mr.

5
00:00:25.795 --> 00:00:27.776
Pendleton lying in bed as before.

6
00:00:30.552 --> 00:00:32.773
But this time he smiled when she sat down.

7
00:00:33.853 --> 00:00:38.654
"You must be a very forgiving person to visit after the way I've treated you," Mr.

8
00:00:38.694 --> 00:00:39.454
Pendleton said.

9
00:00:39.474 --> 00:00:43.256
"I apologize for my rudeness when you brought the beef stew.

10
00:00:44.596 --> 00:00:46.977
And I've never thanked you for helping me when I broke my leg.

11
00:00:47.437 --> 00:00:47.817
Thank you!"

12
00:00:49.437 --> 00:00:52.078
"I was glad to help you," Pollyanna said.

13
00:00:52.098 --> 00:00:55.879
"I mean, I wasn't glad your leg was broken."

14
00:00:55.899 --> 00:00:59.400
"I understand what you meant."

15
00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.001
Mr. Pendleton smiled again.

16
00:01:02.021 --> 00:01:06.722
"You were brave that day in the woods, and the stew was delicious.

17
00:01:07.882 --> 00:01:10.383
Is there any more today that Aunt Polly didn't send?"

18
00:01:12.043 --> 00:01:15.404
Pollyanna's eyes widened at the reminder of Aunt Polly's scolding.

19
00:01:15.424 --> 00:01:17.425
"No, sir."

20
00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.766
Mr. Pendleton stared straight ahead, lost in thought.

21
00:01:24.107 --> 00:01:25.447
At last he sighed.

22
00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:28.168
"I didn't send for you to watch me mope.

23
00:01:29.824 --> 00:01:32.625
Go into the library—you know, the big room with the telephone.

24
00:01:33.886 --> 00:01:36.447
You'll find a wooden box in the cabinet with glass doors.

25
00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:37.547
Bring it here, please."

26
00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:44.790
A few minutes later, Pollyanna returned with the box.

27
00:01:46.611 --> 00:01:48.872
It was full of interesting things that Mr.

28
00:01:48.912 --> 00:01:50.853
Pendleton had picked up during his travels.

29
00:01:52.313 --> 00:01:57.996
He had an entertaining story about every item, including an intricately carved chess set.

30
00:01:59.232 --> 00:02:03.953
They also talked about Pollyanna's life with Aunt Polly as well as her former home out West.

31
00:02:05.214 --> 00:02:07.554
Much too soon, it was time for Pollyanna to leave.

32
00:02:07.574 --> 00:02:12.256
"I want you to visit me often," Mr.

33
00:02:12.296 --> 00:02:13.016
Pendleton said.

34
00:02:13.036 --> 00:02:17.797
"I'm lonely, and there's another reason His voice trailed off.

35
00:02:17.817 --> 00:02:22.819
"When I first learned who you are, I didn't want to see you again.

36
00:02:24.059 --> 00:02:26.480
You reminded me of something I've tried to forget for years.

37
00:02:28.728 --> 00:02:31.850
But then the more I tried to forget, the more I remembered.

38
00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:34.812
So now I want you to come.

39
00:02:35.593 --> 00:02:35.933
Will you?"

40
00:02:35.953 --> 00:02:39.275
"Of course, Mr.

41
00:02:39.315 --> 00:02:44.219
Pendleton." Pollyanna's eyes were filled with sympathy for the sad-faced man.

42
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:50.303
That evening after supper, Pollyanna sat in the backyard, talking with Nancy.

43
00:02:50.323 --> 00:02:53.125
"I can't believe Mr.

44
00:02:53.165 --> 00:02:57.048
Pendleton showed you all those things and told you stories about them."

45
00:02:58.388 --> 00:03:00.309
Nancy shook her head in amazement.

46
00:03:00.329 --> 00:03:06.332
"He's usually so grumpy—if he even bothers to speak."

47
00:03:07.693 --> 00:03:09.634
Pollyanna quickly defended her new friend.

48
00:03:09.654 --> 00:03:12.916
"People wouldn't think he's so bad if they knew him."

49
00:03:16.358 --> 00:03:17.919
Nancy swatted away a fly.

50
00:03:17.939 --> 00:03:21.481
"I don't understand why he's so interested in you.

51
00:03:23.282 --> 00:03:27.424
I mean, no offense, but he's not someone who likes children."

52
00:03:28.652 --> 00:03:29.593
Pollyanna smiled.

53
00:03:29.613 --> 00:03:31.734
"He didn't like me right away.

54
00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:36.637
Just today he admitted that, at first, he didn't want to see me again.

55
00:03:37.777 --> 00:03:43.941
I reminded him of something he wanted to forget and—" "Something he wanted to forget?"

56
00:03:45.122 --> 00:03:46.843
Nancy leaned forward with excitement.

57
00:03:46.863 --> 00:03:48.384
"What was it?"

58
00:03:48.404 --> 00:03:50.965
"He didn't say."

59
00:03:50.985 --> 00:03:53.066
"A mystery!"

60
00:03:53.447 --> 00:03:55.248
Nancy said in an awestruck voice.

61
00:03:56.296 --> 00:03:59.017
"Just like in the mystery novels I love to read.

62
00:03:59.938 --> 00:04:01.958
Only this is a real-life mystery!

63
00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:05.500
Tell me every little detail."

64
00:04:07.681 --> 00:04:11.703
So Pollyanna told everything she could remember from the first time she met Mr.

65
00:04:11.743 --> 00:04:13.223
Pendleton until that day.

66
00:04:13.243 --> 00:04:19.946
"He didn't want to see you again after he learned you were Miss Polly's niece, right?"

67
00:04:20.286 --> 00:04:20.906
Nancy said.

68
00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:24.048
"Yes, that's what he said today."

69
00:04:25.356 --> 00:04:29.697
"And he acted strange when you said Miss Polly didn't want him to think she'd sent the stew?"

70
00:04:31.058 --> 00:04:33.218
Nancy was growing more excited by the minute.

71
00:04:34.679 --> 00:04:38.100
"Yes, but—" "I've got it!"

72
00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.761
Nancy looked around to make sure nobody else was listening.

73
00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:45.362
"He and Miss Polly were sweethearts!"

74
00:04:46.962 --> 00:04:49.883
"What? Aunt Polly doesn't even like him.

75
00:04:51.003 --> 00:04:53.704
She didn't want him to think the beef stew came from her."

76
00:04:55.344 --> 00:04:58.265
"Tom told me that she had a sweetheart long ago.

77
00:04:58.285 --> 00:05:02.046
They had an argument and broke off their engagement.

78
00:05:03.347 --> 00:05:05.467
Tom said the man still lives in town!"

79
00:05:06.848 --> 00:05:09.928
Pollyanna still wasn't convinced, so Nancy pressed on.

80
00:05:09.948 --> 00:05:13.389
"Mr. Pendleton said you reminded him of someone.

81
00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:16.470
It has to be Miss Polly!"

82
00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:21.692
"But if they loved each other, they would have made up years ago."

83
00:05:23.644 --> 00:05:25.746
"Sometimes sweethearts can be stubborn."

84
00:05:26.827 --> 00:05:28.829
Nancy had a dreamy look on her face.

85
00:05:28.849 --> 00:05:35.476
"Wouldn't it be wonderful if you taught them the Glad Game and they got back together?"
